  "content": {
    "id": "p22-q9-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "9",
    "prompt": "For each pair of equations, solve for $x$ and $y$ using the most appropriate method.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 3,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p22-q9-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$$\\begin{aligned}x+2y&=6\\\\3x-y&=2\\end{aligned}$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\frac{10}{7},\\ y=\\frac{16}{7}$.",
          "worked": "Elimination: double the second equation and add the first.\n$$\\begin{align*}6x-2y&=4\\\\(x+2y)+(6x-2y)&=6+4\\\\7x&=10\\\\x&=\\frac{10}{7}\\end{align*}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}y&=3\\left(\\frac{10}{7}\\right)-2\\\\y&=\\frac{16}{7}\\end{align*}$$\nCheck: $\\frac{10}{7}+2\\left(\\frac{16}{7}\\right)=6$ and $3\\left(\\frac{10}{7}\\right)-\\frac{16}{7}=2$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 76
      },
      {
        "id": "p22-q9-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$$\\begin{aligned}2x-5y&=10\\\\5x-2y&=12\\end{aligned}$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\frac{40}{21},\\ y=-\\frac{26}{21}$.\n\nMultiply the equations to match the coefficients of $y$, then subtract.",
          "worked": "Elimination: multiply the first equation by 2 and the second by 5.\n$$\\begin{align*}4x-10y&=20\\\\25x-10y&=60\\\\(25x-10y)-(4x-10y)&=60-20\\\\21x&=40\\\\x&=\\frac{40}{21}\\end{align*}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}2\\left(\\frac{40}{21}\\right)-5y&=10\\\\-5y&=\\frac{130}{21}\\\\y&=-\\frac{26}{21}\\end{align*}$$\nCheck: $\\frac{80}{21}+\\frac{130}{21}=10$ and $\\frac{200}{21}+\\frac{52}{21}=12$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 92
      },
      {
        "id": "p22-q9-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$$\\begin{aligned}y&=3-2x\\\\2x-5y&=12\\end{aligned}$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\frac94,\\ y=-\\frac32$.",
          "worked": "Substitution:\n$$\\begin{align*}2x-5(3-2x)&=12\\\\2x-15+10x&=12\\\\12x&=27\\\\x&=\\frac94\\end{align*}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}y&=3-2\\left(\\frac94\\right)\\\\y&=-\\frac32\\end{align*}$$\nCheck: $2\\left(\\frac94\\right)-5\\left(-\\frac32\\right)=12$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 76
      },
      {
        "id": "p22-q9-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$$\\begin{aligned}y&=2x+5\\\\y&=-3x-7\\end{aligned}$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=-\\frac{12}{5},\\ y=\\frac15$.",
          "worked": "Equate the expressions for $y$.\n$$\\begin{align*}2x+5&=-3x-7\\\\5x&=-12\\\\x&=-\\frac{12}{5}\\end{align*}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}y&=2\\left(-\\frac{12}{5}\\right)+5\\\\y&=\\frac15\\end{align*}$$\nCheck: $-3\\left(-\\frac{12}{5}\\right)-7=\\frac15$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 68
      },
      {
        "id": "p22-q9-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$$\\begin{aligned}x&=1-2y\\\\5y-2x&=10\\end{aligned}$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=-\\frac53,\\ y=\\frac43$.",
          "worked": "Substitution:\n$$\\begin{align*}5y-2(1-2y)&=10\\\\5y-2+4y&=10\\\\9y&=12\\\\y&=\\frac43\\end{align*}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}x&=1-2\\left(\\frac43\\right)\\\\x&=-\\frac53\\end{align*}$$\nCheck: $5\\left(\\frac43\\right)-2\\left(-\\frac53\\right)=10$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 76
      },
      {
        "id": "p22-q9-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$$\\begin{aligned}x&=5y+3\\\\x&=3y-2\\end{aligned}$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=-\\frac{19}{2},\\ y=-\\frac52$.",
          "worked": "Equate the expressions for $x$.\n$$\\begin{align*}5y+3&=3y-2\\\\2y&=-5\\\\y&=-\\frac52\\end{align*}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}x&=5\\left(-\\frac52\\right)+3\\\\x&=-\\frac{19}{2}\\end{align*}$$\nCheck: $3\\left(-\\frac52\\right)-2=-\\frac{19}{2}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 68
      }
